0..72 Comment "// A body whose result is a function value may end in a bare lambda. The"
73..149 Comment "// result type is a box, and the checker reads the lambda as that box, which"
150..227 Comment "// the body returns. The core is the one a written `return` gives. The lambda"
228..304 Comment "// stands at the end of a body, after a `let`, at the end of a block, and in"
305..328 Comment "// each arm of a match."
329..331 Comment "//"
332..408 Comment "// Two cases keep their `return`. A box whose computation is no function has"
409..484 Comment "// no lambda to read. A lambda whose expected type is unknown has no box to"
485..528 Comment "// read against, so it stays a computation."
529..531 Comment "//"
532..547 Comment "// - see: #6390"
